 // Draws the rally summary screen: the event banner and the menu path, the
 // stage name with its distance, surface and severity, the record time of the
 // selected stage and one row per stage of the rally with its record time.
+// match 88%: same calls, constants and block structure as the original; only
+// MSVC 6's frame layout differs. The original keeps x/limit in [esp+0x10],
+// column/count in [esp+0x14], table in [esp+0x18], width/whole/frac/n in
+// [esp+0x1c] and country in [esp+0x24]; this build keeps whole/limit in
+// [esp+0x10], x/width in [esp+0x14], column/count/n in [esp+0x18], country in
+// [esp+0x1c], table in [esp+0x20] and frac in [esp+0x24], which is also why
+// count+2 lands in EBP here instead of being an `add ebx,2` in place, and why
+// the loop counter is not spilled. Reordering or renaming the locals does not
+// move the slots (the allocator derives them from the live ranges), so every
+// remaining mismatch is a frame slot or the register holding it.
